From 7d71ff36911de106d0e6cf42ce4c9f4ce4186450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fixes <fix@helpdesk>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 02:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: auth, user creation, customer user, password
 hashing, JWT, CORS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backend fixes:
- auth.py: fix duplicate login_for_access_token function name (agent and
  customer routes had the same Python function name; Python was silently
  dropping the agent /token endpoint)
- auth.py: rename customer route function to customer_login to avoid override
- auth.py: replace SHA256 password verification with proper bcrypt via passlib
- auth.py: fix token expiry from 3 min → 60 min (configurable via env)
- auth.py: move SECRET_KEY / ALGORITHM to settings (config.py)
- auth.py: fix Optional[str] type hints (was using deprecated 'str or None')
- middleware: fix JWT key mismatch — token encodes 'user_type' but middleware
  was reading 'usertype'; customer users were always routed as 'agent'
- middleware: read SECRET_KEY from settings instead of hardcoding it
- utils.py: replace SHA256 with bcrypt (passlib CryptContext); add
  verify_password helper
- config.py: add SECRET_KEY, ALGORITHM, ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES,
  CORS_ORIGINS, DATABASE_URL settings — all configurable via .env
- db/session.py: read DATABASE_URL from config instead of hardcoding creds
- main.py: read CORS origins from config instead of hardcoded local IP
- customeruser_controller.py: fix Delete_customer_cache using wrong
  'user:' prefix instead of 'customeruser:'
- customeruser_controller.py: fix get_all_preferences called with login
  (str) when CustomerPreferences.user_id is FK to customer_user.id (int)
- customeruser_controller.py: fix customer_user_update email check — was
  reading from preferences (always empty for CustomerUser); now compares
  directly against existing_user.email on the model
- customeruser_controller.py: fix customer_user_update marking optional
  fields (phone, fax, street, etc.) as required — broke all updates
- customeruser_controller.py: add email_exists(exclude_user_id) to avoid
  false duplicate on self-update
- user_controller.py: fix email_exists to use .exists() query; add
  exclude_user_id to avoid false duplicate on self-update
- user_controller.py: implement is_valid_email with real regex (was 'return True')
- schemas/user.py: make 'mobile' Optional (was required, broke user creation)
- requirements.txt: add pydantic-settings (was missing, caused ImportError
  on fresh install) and email-validator (needed by Pydantic EmailStr)
- add itsm/backend/.env.example for environment configuration
- update .gitignore to exclude .env files (secrets should not be committed)

Frontend fixes:
- customerapiClient.js: use REACT_APP_API_URL env var instead of hardcoded IP
- customerapiClient.js: add 401 interceptor for auto-logout
- agentapiClient.js: use REACT_APP_API_URL env var instead of hardcoded IP
- agentapiClient.js: add 401 interceptor for auto-logout
- AuthService.js: fix customer login using agentapiClient (wrong!) — now uses
  customerapiClient so the correct customeruser_token cookie is attached
- AuthService.js: add agentLogoutApi / customerLogoutApi helpers
- AuthService.js: improve error message to surface backend 'detail' field
- PrivateRoute.js: check cookie as fallback when Redux state is false —
  previously page refresh evicted Redux state and force-redirected logged-in
  users back to the login page even with a valid cookie
- add itsm/frontend/.env.example
